course: dictionary
lesson: 5077
title: Insulation keeps things warm, cool or safe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To insulate something means to cover it with a material that stops heat, cold, sound or electricity from passing through easily. A woolly jumper insulates you: it keeps your warmth in and the cold out. «The ice lid insulates the water below, which stays liquid, so fish and frogs can survive the winter at the bottom.»
explain: Some materials let heat travel through them easily, and some do not. «Metal conducts heat», so «a metal spoon left in hot tea soon has a hot handle, but a wooden spoon does not, because wood insulates.» Conduct means to let heat or electricity travel through.
explain: Electric wires are covered in plastic or rubber. This insulation stops the electricity from getting out, so people do not get a shock. If the covering is damaged, the wire is not insulated any more, so never touch it.
fact: To insulate means to cover something so heat, cold, sound or electricity cannot pass through easily.
fact: Insulators include plastic, rubber, wool, feathers and foam.
fact: «Insulate a house» means to fill walls and roofs with materials that keep heat inside.
fact: An «insulated cup» keeps a drink hot or cold for longer.
fact: Metal conducts heat, but wood insulates.
exercise: «The ice lid insulates the water below.» What does insulates mean here? | Pushes the water up to the top | Turns the water into steam | *Covers and protects, so the water stays liquid | Makes the water freeze solid
exercise: Why does the wooden spoon stay cool in hot tea? | The spoon is too small to hold any heat | *Wood insulates, so the heat does not pass easily to the handle | Wood makes the tea colder | Wood is made of metal
exercise: Why must you never touch a wire whose insulation is damaged? | The wire will become sticky | Wires need touching to start working | *Electricity can get out and could hurt you | The plastic becomes too light to hold
test: Which of these is a good insulator? | Copper wire | Tin can | *Wool | Steel nail
test: Which phrase means a cup that keeps drinks hot or cold for longer? | A tin tray | A conducting spoon | *An insulated cup | A loud cup
exam: Why is foam used to insulate a house? | *It stops heat escaping, so the house stays warm | It makes the house float | It lets electricity into the walls | It conducts heat out quickly
